  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gà nướng xả is chicken marinated in finely minced "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "xa-lemongrass"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "xả "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "and grilled until caramelised. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The marinade forms a fragrant crust on the outside of the chicken while the inside stays juicy. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This recipe serves 4."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Bone-in, skin-on chicken thighs are best for this recipe. They stay juicier on the grill than breast meat and develop a better caramelised crust."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 4,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "chicken-thigh",
              "amount": 8,
              "unit": "whole",
              "prepNote": "bone-in, skin-on",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "chicken"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "lemongrass",
              "amount": 3,
              "unit": "stalks",
              "prepNote": "white part only, finely minced",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "marinade"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "garlic",
              "amount": 4,
              "unit": "cloves",
              "prepNote": "minced",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "marinade"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "shallots",
              "amount": 3,
              "unit": "whole",
              "prepNote": "minced",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "marinade"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "fish-sauce",
              "amount": 3,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "marinade"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "caster-sugar",
              "amount": 2,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "marinade"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "turmeric-ground",
              "amount": 0.5,
              "unit": "tsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "marinade"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "vegetable-oil",
              "amount": 2,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "marinade"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "chilli-red",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "whole",
              "prepNote": "sliced, to serve",
              "isOptional": true,
              "groupLabel": "to serve"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "lime",
              "amount": 2,
              "unit": "whole",
              "prepNote": "cut into wedges",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "to serve"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "coriander-fresh",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "handful",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "to serve"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Score the chicken thighs 2 to 3 times to the bone to help the marinade penetrate."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mix the lemongrass, garlic, shallots, fish sauce, sugar, turmeric, and oil. Rub all over the chicken and into the scores. Marinate for at least 2 hours in the fridge."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Remove the chicken from the fridge 30 minutes before cooking."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat a griddle pan over medium-high heat. Grill the chicken skin-side down for 8 to 10 minutes until the skin is golden and charred in places."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Turn and cook for another 8 to 10 minutes until cooked through. The juices should run clear when pierced near the bone."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "If the outside caramelises before the inside is cooked, transfer to a 200°C oven for 10 minutes to finish."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Rest for 5 minutes. Serve with lime wedges, fresh coriander, "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                        "attrs": {
                          "termSlug": "tuong-ot"
                        }
                      }
                    ],
                    "text": "tương ớt "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "chilli sauce, and steamed rice."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The lemongrass in the marinade burns quickly on the grill.",
              "cause": "Lemongrass fibres char quickly at high temperatures.",
              "fix": "Scrape off most of the marinade solids before grilling. The flavour has already penetrated the meat and the excess will just burn."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The chicken skin is flabby and pale.",
              "cause": "The pan was not hot enough before the chicken went in.",
              "fix": "Preheat the griddle until very hot before adding the chicken. Place it skin-side down and do not move it for at least 5 minutes."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The chicken is raw at the bone.",
              "cause": "The thighs were too thick or the heat was too high, cooking the outside but not the inside.",
              "fix": "Finish thick thighs in the oven at 200°C for 10 minutes after grilling. Use an instant-read thermometer - the centre should read 75°C."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Lemongrass chicken is a staple of Vietnamese street food and home cooking. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "It is cooked on charcoal grills at outdoor markets throughout the country. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Lemongrass is used in similar grilled chicken dishes across all of Southeast Asia. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "In Vietnam, it is a common dish to cook at home for family dinners. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The bright turmeric colour makes it one of the most visually striking dishes on any street food stall."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
